  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.48–0.65) vastly outperform image-only models (0.21–0.23), and the best RNA configuration is scvi_n200 + multiprofile (avgpool: 0.650, transformer: 0.653). The critical unresolved question is whether adding the image modality provides any complementary signal on top of the already-strong RNA representation, or whether it introduces noise. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly extends the best RNA-only setup (config_005) by adding resnet50 image features with simple concat fusion, isolating the effect of the image modality while keeping all other design choices at their best-evidenced settings. If it matches config_005 (~0.65), image adds no value and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side refinements; if it substantially exceeds 0.65, multimodal fusion is worth further exploration. Using the simpler resnet50 and concat fusion minimizes confounds and makes the comparison clean. This is the highest-information next step because it resolves the single largest remaining uncertainty—whether the image channel is worth incorporating at all—before committing budget to more complex multimodal variants."
}

